compose() applies _apply_phenotype_transform() to HARD domain/situation packets,
mutating/removing HARD directive content such as examples/rationale.

This script imports the real module, reads the real compose() source via inspect,
monkeypatches only the module's loading seams to provide controlled HARD packets,
snapshots those packets before compose(), runs the real compose() path, and raises
AssertionError / prints FALSIFIED iff a HARD domain or situation packet is
phenotype-transformed.
